    def reset(self, **kwargs):

        """ This keyword is used to do reset operations. Multiple operations are supported in same keyword.
        *ADMIN*
        | *Supported operations* |
        | *Operation* | *OAM* |
        | reset_admin | ADMIN |
        | reset_bts_rad_parameters | ADMIN |
        | reset_rad_debug_parameters | ADMIN |
        | reset_configuration | ADMIN |
        | reset_rat | ADMIN |
        | reset_to_test_dedicated | ADMIN |
        | reset_unit | ADMIN |
        | reset_bts | ADMIN |
        | site | MEGAZONE |

        *COMMON*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Comments* | *Valid For* |
        | operation | *Mandatory* | Operation from the above list | ADMIN |
        | alias | default | Name of the execution context | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | timeout | 300 | Timeout for the operation | Both CU and ADMIN |

        *reset_admin:*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |


        *reset_bts_rad_parameters:*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | component | *Mandatory* | BTS system component number | ADMIN |
        | params | Mandatory | RAD parameters string | ADMIN |

        *_reset_rad_debug_parameters*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | name | Mandatory | (str) - Parameter name | ADMIN |
        |  |  | or ALL to reset all parameters. |  |
        | domain | Mandatory | (str) - Domain name | ADMIN |
        |  |  | Pass only if name is NOT 'ALL'. |  |
        | detailed_output | False | return full request response when True. |  |

        *reset_configuration:*

        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | remove_operator_certificates | False | (bool) - Remove operator certificates | ADMIN |
        |  |  | For release SBTS23R1 and below |  |
        | remove_user_account_credentials | False | (bool) - Remove user account credentials | ADMIN |
        |  |  | For release SBTS23R1 and below |  |
        | resetType | ConfigurationWithDNRSW | (str) - Type of the performed reset. Added via CNI-70685. | ADMIN |
        |  |  | One of: ['Configuration']. For release SBTS23R2 and above |  |
        | detailed_output | False |  (bool) - return full request response when True. |  |

        *reset_rat:*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | rat |  *Mandatory* for 'reset_rat' operation |  | ADMIN |
        | verify_bts | True | True if bts status to be verified after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | should_be_onair | True | True if BTS should be onair, else False | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | wait_for | 300 | Time to wait(seconds) before checking for status after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |

        *reset_unit:*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | dist_name | *Mandatory* for 'reset_unit' operation | | ADMIN |
        | reset_type | *Mandatory* for 'reset_unit' operation | Soft/Hard/Warm reset | ADMIN |
        | force_radio_reset | None | (bool) - optional parameter to force radio reset | ADMIN |
        |  |  | 'forceRadioReset' is only for RMOD|ASIRMOD. | ADMIN |
        | verify_bts | True | True if bts status to be verified after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | rat |  rat dist name |  | ADMIN |
        | should_be_onair | True | True if BTS should be onair, else False | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | wait_for | 300 | Time to wait(seconds) before checking for status after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | detailed_output  | False | (bool) -  return full request response when True | ADMIN |

        *reset_bts:*
        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Description* |  *Valid For* |
        | rat |  *Mandatory* for 'reset_rat' operation |  | ADMIN |
        | verify_bts | True | True if bts status to be verified after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | should_be_onair | True | True if BTS should be onair, else False | Both CU and ADMIN |
        | wait_for | 300 | Time to wait(seconds) before checking for status after reset | Both CU and ADMIN |

        *Returns:*
        | Admin | Return value varies with the supported operation. |
        |   | Refer to https://docs.taf.nsn-rdnet.net/taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin/ |

        *Raises:*
        | Admin | AttributeError, if operation type is not supported |
        |   | PingTestFailedException, if ping test fails while verifying "Reset BTS" |

        *Examples:*
        *Reset BTS and verify BTS status for only LTE cells*

        * Admin *
        | Reset  | operation=reset_rat | rat=LTE |

        """

        return Reset().reset(**kwargs)

