    def query_admin_infomodel(self, **kwargs):
        """
         _*Query Admin Infomodel*_  Run query against InfoModel and return its result.Keyword will
            wait until the result is successful or timeout seconds pass.

        *Usage*:
         Query Admin Infomodel   <query>   <api_version>   <timeout>   <alias>
                <extended_result=False>    <allow_negative_result>    <str_format>


        | *arguments* | *comment* | *default value* |
        | *query*  | Query expression on InfoModel. |
        | *api_version* | Optional argument. Query api version. Currently available api version is
            "v1" | v1 |
        | *timeout* | Timeout value. | 10 |
        | *alias* | Name of execution context. | default |
        | *extend_result* |  Optional argument. Extend result with additional data like query data
            timestamp. | ${False} |
        | *allow_negative_result* |  Optional argument. Allow negative query result to be returned
            instead of InfoModelQueryTimeoutException. | ${False} |
        | *str_format* |  Optional Argument and is used only for query = "get param". Returns
            result if string format is True and result dictionary has one key else dictionary is
            returned. | ${True} |
        | rat | At least one of the RATs is Mandatory eg. lte/wcdma/gsm etc. | common |

        *Note*:
        Keyword performs exactly same as what Query Infomodel keyword of UTE's ute_admin_infomodel
            library does. In addition to it this keyword performs another operation "get param".
        Details on queries of UTE library's Keyword Query Infomodel is present in the link :
            http://doc.ute.inside.nsn.com/packages/ute_admin_infomodel/
            interfaces/ute_admin_infomodel.html#query-infomodel .
        Details on query "get param is present below.

        | *Query*  | *Syntax* | *example* | *description* |
        | *get param* | get param DIST_NAME:PARAMETER1:PARAMETER2:PARAMETER3 | keyword is used to
            get a parameter from bts. If value of PARAMETER1 for DIST_NAME contains a dictionary,
            then PARAMETER2 is fetched from it. Similarly, PARAMETER3 is fetched if value of
            PARAMETER2 is a dictionary. |

        DIST_NAME supports regular expression. To know how to use regular expression in DIST_NAME,
        check the link
        http://doc.ute.inside.nsn.com/packages/ute_admin_infomodel/
        interfaces/ute_admin_infomodel.html#query-infomodel

        *Example*
         | *keyword*  | *query* | *timeout* | *alias* | *extend_result* | *allow_negative_result* |
            *str_format* |
         | *Query Admin Infomodel*  | *query=get param /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1
            /MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-0:cPlane:ipV4AddressDN1:localIpAddr* | | | | | |
         | *Query Admin Infomodel*  | *query=get param /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1
            /MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-*:cPlane:ipV4AddressDN1:localIpAddr* | *timeout=30* |
            *alias=default* | *extend_result=${False}* | *allow_negetive_result=${False} |
            *str_format=${False}* |
         | *Query Admin Infomodel*  | *query=get list /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1
            /MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-**  | *timeout=30* | *alias=default* |
            *extend_result=${False}* | *allow_negetive_result=${False} | |

        """

        return Parameters().query_admin_infomodel(**kwargs)

